{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul","id":1233307,"title":"Caul-ing for help: Solars in the Caul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-08T16:50:59-07:00","id":1233307,"title":"Caul-ing for help: Solars in the Caul","content":"My players have decided that the best way to destroy the guild and conquer Lookshy is to go to the Caul, and help/recruit a lunar/beastman army. What do I do now @_@? Do we know anything about the Caul? and would Feng-Yi open for a Solar pilgrimage, or just Lunars and DBs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T17:00:52-07:00","id":1233310,"title":"","content":"If you don't like that idea much, help establish the sheer distance that place is. That is thousands and thousands of miles away. You could easily have them stumble into 3-4 lunar groups while trying to get down to the coast, and fight half the realm beforecthey even make it out West.<br /> <br /> If you like the idea, i would have them deal with being cast in the role of kingmakers rather than kings for this. They choose a lunar to support and get them through the pilgrimage. Maybe a rival or subordiante of the Black Lion unless you want to give them an easier win with how the Black Lion is currently described","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","user":"Cryo-Seraph","date":". 07-08-2018, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T18:06:47-07:00","id":1233318,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to remind y'all of the sheer distance between Lookshy and the Caul; would a more local source of aid not be more preferable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T18:56:22-07:00","id":1233322,"title":"","content":"Local Lunars are much more likely to help the Solars destroy local rivals than the Caul Lunars are likely to care about whatever is going on so far away from the Caul.<br /> <br /> Why would I go to Australia for help with a problem in Texas when I can go to another city in Texas to find people much more predisposed to care about Texan problems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T19:02:30-07:00","id":1233323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233322#post1233322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would I go to Australia for help with a problem in Texas when I can go to another city in Texas to find people much more predisposed to care about Texan problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially in a pre-industrial, pre-Internet society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T19:29:29-07:00","id":1233327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul#post1233307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know anything about the Caul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the Kickstarter preview? Not much. And even when it gets its full chapter, I have a feeling that a lot of what it might contain is left to the imagination of the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> For the time being, I think a particularly worthwhile purpose that the Caul might serve is being a location where the game has fiat to introduce a wide variety of particularly odd magic without needing to deal with a question of how it might have impacted the setting by saying that it hasn't (by virtue of things like being hemmed in by the Realm and the ocean, and the island having disappeared for centuries).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">would Feng-Yi open for a Solar pilgrimage, or just Lunars and DBs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the importance that Feng-Yi holds to those two would be diminished by extending it to Solars. Instead, I think it's worth approaching from the direction of the pilgrimage being a thing that emerges from the island's power (hence, having alternative forms hidden away in the wilderness), rather than being the crux of it.<br /> <br /> As for the distance... this is an instance where I'm seeing certain realistic considerations bowing down to be a stepping stone for pulp and mythic exaggeration. It's Portuguese sailors trying to find Prester John because they think he'll be a vital ally against the Islamic world in the east. I'm having a picture of somebody finding the local powers incapable or untrustworthy enough to prefer journeying halfway around the world to recruit forces that they think are more up to the task; like if European invasion of the Americas was predicated on an Aztec rebel making a lone voyage to cross the Atlantic and bring some conquistadors home.<br /> <br /> Not especially likely, but I think that some grandeur can effectively override that sometimes and produce a compelling result. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T19:45:11-07:00","id":1233328,"title":"","content":"On that subject, is anyone else unhappy that we might not get a concrete, known benefit for Lunar Exalted who complete the pilgrimage while controlling all five shrine cities?<br /> <br /> I know it's hard to think of something of worth analogous to a Dragon-Blood's next child being guaranteed to Exalt, but that doesn't seem like an excuse to not try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T20:19:51-07:00","id":1233331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233328#post1233328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that subject, is anyone else unhappy that we might not get a concrete, known benefit for Lunar Exalted who complete the pilgrimage while controlling all five shrine cities?<br /> <br /> I know it's hard to think of something of worth analogous to a Dragon-Blood's next child being guaranteed to Exalt, but that doesn't seem like an excuse to not try.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I agree its kind of annoying. Right now the Caul feels like a really cool Dragonblooded setting that happens to use Lunars as a enemy incidentally. Really hoping fangs at the gate expands on why you would actually want to play a lunar on the Caul as opposed to somewhere else in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:58:51-07:00","id":1233349,"title":"","content":"<i>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</i> will have a section covering the Caul from the Lunar perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T07:52:07-07:00","id":1233420,"title":"","content":"With Wyld Taint taken out behind the shed and shot, and with the Lost Castes being deliberately discarded by the Lunar Exalted, the most obvious options for the pilgrimage\u2019s reward don\u2019t exist.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded get to make a whole other Exalt. That\u2019s amazing. It\u2019s powerful without directly empowering a Terrestrial. <br /> <br /> A Lunar cannot give birth to a new Lunar Exaltation. A Lunar should not be able to mark his or her next child for Lunar Exaltation. <br /> <br /> I can\u2019t bring myself to like the idea of the Lunar securing a Terrestrial Exaltation for her next child, either.<br /> <br /> Ensuring that one\u2019s child will be a powerful Moontouched seems weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T08:17:53-07:00","id":1233425,"title":"","content":"I think it's either got to be something massively different, or that the benefit is that they stop the Dragonblood doing it. Which is something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T08:22:42-07:00","id":1233427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233420#post1233420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Wyld Taint taken out behind the shed and shot, and with the Lost Castes being deliberately discarded by the Lunar Exalted, the most obvious options for the pilgrimage\u2019s reward don\u2019t exist.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded get to make a whole other Exalt. That\u2019s amazing. It\u2019s powerful without directly empowering a Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> A Lunar cannot give birth to a new Lunar Exaltation. A Lunar should not be able to mark his or her next child for Lunar Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t bring myself to like the idea of the Lunar securing a Terrestrial Exaltation for her next child, either.<br /> <br /> Ensuring that one\u2019s child will be a powerful Moontouched seems weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're doing it again; that thing where you alternately assume the worst, and act with unprovoked and unwarranted hostility towards somebody that was on the same side as you.<br /> <br /> I mean Jesus Christ, person; you express a hope that the books won't leave the Lunar side of it un-fleshed out, one of the developers comes in to say that the Lunars book will cover their side of it, and then you leap to, what, doomsaying? Betting that the result will suck?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T08:26:33-07:00","id":1233429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233425#post1233425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the benefit is that they stop the Dragonblood doing it. Which is something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> something, but it's not a thing that warrants an idea that the Caul's shrines become actively attuned to Lunar Essence, rather than simply being denied to the Dragon Blooded. Nor does it really make sense with a backstory in which Luna has an association with the place that makes it sacred to Lunars.<br /> <br /> Given the way that the place is built up, it has to have an importance to Lunars when they're <i>not</i> in conflict with major Dragon Blooded powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T08:39:55-07:00","id":1233433,"title":"","content":"Yeah, after writing that, I thought about it a bit more, and I think that would be uninspiring and un...spiritual? Unreligious rather.<br /> <br /> The whole point of having shrines for a crusade over is that they're of great significance to both sides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Shrines make me overtly think of something religious (such as more easily praying to Luna or her under-spirits), but I'm not sure that works very well either. A blessing from Luna seems obvious, but what?<br /> It probably needs to be something inherent to Lunars, but as Sunder said, there's not a lot of obvious issues.<br /> <br /> Perhaps something about Heart's Blood? Or raising their essence easier? A feeling of union with the essence of Luna? It doesn't necessarily have to be mechanical, though if not, it may not seem significant to Lunar players the way having DB kids is obviously significant to DB players.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, anyone who has ideas feel free to share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-09-2018, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T09:13:09-07:00","id":1233441,"title":"","content":"I'd like to think the nature of the blessing might differ based on the Lunar who completes the pilgrimage; one might get a new suite of forms, those of animals long lost to the mists of history, while another might achieve some other unique benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T09:40:24-07:00","id":1233448,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the responses!<br /> <br /> Quick backstory, the Solar party exalted on the blessed isle, and during their various misadventures (including an upcoming attempted sacking of the city of Arjuf) a Lunar NPC is attempting to help underground railroad them off the isle. When asked if she would care to join them on their rampage across the threshold, she declined and said she had business in the Caul. That was when the party decided to just follow her to the Caul...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233433#post1233433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of having shrines for a crusade over is that they're of great significance to both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, if this is going to be a holy land that Lunars and DB are crusading in, it should be <i>important</i> to both of them. Though I like the idea that what the Lunars discover if they finish the pilgrimage isn't exactly what they wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> Given that the name, &quot;The Caul&quot;, has so many birth and luck connotations, the favorable birth blessing for the DB makes great sense. Reaffirming Gaia's love for her children and blessing them with children, great, good, done.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if the Lunar pilgrimage would reaffirm Gaia's love for Luna and her chosen? And if so, how would that manifest? Elemental blessings?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T10:36:43-07:00","id":1233466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233427#post1233427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're doing it again; that thing where you alternately assume the worst, and act with unprovoked and unwarranted hostility towards somebody that was on the same side as you.<br /> <br /> I mean Jesus Christ, person; you express a hope that the books won't leave the Lunar side of it un-fleshed out, one of the developers comes in to say that the Lunars book will cover their side of it, and then you leap to, what, doomsaying? Betting that the result will suck?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re doing it again; assuming the worst of my behavior because you think you have seen it before.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t even responding to Eric. I was simply putting myself to the challenge.<br /> <br /> It struck me as dishonest to say that someone should try to answer a difficult question without myself trying to answer the difficult question. I wanted to acknowledge that the puzzle was a difficult one to solve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T13:41:12-07:00","id":1233493,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's my bad. I unreservedly apologise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:02:46-07:00","id":1233500,"title":"","content":"Considering the war between Lunars and Dragon Blooded, simply keeping the shrines out of Dragon Blooded hands is worthwhile in and of itself. Still, presumably the Lunars would get some kind of benefit from these shrines or else they would have tried to destroy them, since destroying infrastucture to deny it to the Dragon Blooded is their typical modus operandi, and would probably be a lot easier and safer than engaging in a protected war if the only goal was to keep the Dragon Blooded from having access to them.<br /> <br /> So if the Lunars are fighting and guarding these shrines rather than simply destroying them, presumably the shrines provide the Lunars with something of value to outweigh the possibility that someday the Dragon Blooded might reacquire these shrines. <br /> <br /> According to the core book, the Shrines were dedicated to the Five Elemental Dragons but Luna and Gaia also traveled on the Caul as well. Perhaps the Shrines to the Elemental Dragons were constructed during the Shogunate and were built on top of older Shrines to the Lunars. Meanwhile the present day Lunars are digging out or repairing those old Lunar shrines, and perhaps those give some kind of bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:06:51-07:00","id":1233502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233493#post1233493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's my bad. I unreservedly apologise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apology accepted. To be fair, my intent would have been much clearer if I\u2019d explained my reason before undertaking the challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:11:48-07:00","id":1233503,"title":"","content":"What if a Lunar didn\u2019t get an Exalted child from the pilgrimage, but a companion? A Gaia to their Luna.<br /> <br /> A mate to take the place of a long-lost Solar Mate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:27:13-07:00","id":1233509,"title":"","content":"Maybe you can change your totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T15:40:29-07:00","id":1233530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233509#post1233509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you can change your totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we\u2019re told Lunars can already do that. That\u2019s what Chimerism is, now.<br /> <br /> Also, if Lunars can do personas somewhere between Terrestrial and Solar competence, it\u2019s likely to include the ability to give a persona a different Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T16:55:04-07:00","id":1233544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233530#post1233530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we\u2019re told Lunars can already do that. That\u2019s what Chimerism is, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, technically correct. Clarification! Maybe you can wholly change your totem from a singular, natural animal into a different single, natural animal.<br /> <br /> I don't mean that to be condescending, just 100% clear on what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> Thinking more about it, I would definitely think that it has something to do with their shapeshifting, since part of what makes the Caul sacred is the intersection between Luna and Gaia, and animalistic shapeshifting is now given a mythic basis as a tribute from Luna to Gaia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T17:36:08-07:00","id":1233554,"title":"","content":"What do we know about the black lion? And do y\u2019all think solars would be seen as welcome assistance to finally bring the realm to heel? Or unwanted glory stealing vain madmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T17:42:46-07:00","id":1233556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233554#post1233554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about the black lion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much: he's younger than one might expect (less than a thousand), has a reputation for coming back now matter how often he's attested to having died, highly respected among Lunars for fighting to reclaim the Caul and managing to cheat death so often, and likes to announce his return or the commencement of his campaigns with very loud roars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And do y\u2019all think solars would be seen as welcome assistance to finally bring the realm to heel? Or unwanted glory stealing vain madmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we've gotten a specification for Oka, and either is plausible, so it comes down to how hard you want to make things for your group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T17:53:09-07:00","id":1233558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233503#post1233503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if a Lunar didn\u2019t get an Exalted child from the pilgrimage, but a companion? A Gaia to their Luna.<br /> <br /> A mate to take the place of a long-lost Solar Mate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, maybe if a Lunar completes the pilgrimage with someone they care deeply for, the Lunar gains the effects of the bond for that person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T18:20:47-07:00","id":1233561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233558#post1233558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, maybe if a Lunar completes the pilgrimage with someone they care deeply for, the Lunar gains the effects of the bond for that person?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of a Gaian behemoth-person spontaneously created by whatever numinous force/creature exists at the end of the journey, actually.<br /> <br /> Presumably, the original bonds were forged with sorcery. If not simply Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> But in any case, the &quot;new mate&quot; thing has something going for it: If the Lunar Exalted really haven't controlled the Caul for a while even before the Usurpation, it could be because few Lunars cared to go on the pilgrimage to get a powerful mate because the Solar Exalted were right there.<br /> <br /> When the Solar Exalted failed to return, a lot of Lunars might have stormed the Caul looking to fill a void while also hitting the Dragon-Blooded where it hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T18:55:30-07:00","id":1233570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1233307-caul-ing-for-help-solars-in-the-caul?p=1233561#post1233561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more of a Gaian behemoth-person spontaneously created by whatever numinous force/creature exists at the end of the journey, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sticking with that idea, maybe if you take someone who already cares deeply for you, they get twisted and changed into a Gaian behemoth-person? I'd honestly be a bit weary of the the universe creating an individual whose purpose of existence is to be a mate to the Lunar. Admittedly that's not an totally uncommon trope in fiction but it also carries some issues with the way that would be perceived by a lot of people in the general community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T19:36:03-07:00","id":1233579,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I wonder if there might be some kind of &quot;shared control&quot; option if a mixed group of Dragon-Bloods and Lunars ever agreed on joint occupation of the shrines. Maybe it sends a beacon out into the Wyld to call Gaia back to Creation? &quot;Coast is clear, we agree on something, everything's (presumably) okay now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T20:12:47-07:00","id":1233584,"title":"","content":"Love the ideas! I'm thinking of doing Feng-Yi as a sort of Brigadoon/Shambhala full of citizen Gaian behemoth persons, sort of a celestial tier Dragon Blooded. When the doors open for a DB they may enter but none of the Gaians may leave, lest the city vanish forever, so the bless their visitor with fertility, to renew the blood of dragons. But Gaia's love for Luna, allows Lunars who complete her pilgrimage to find a mate/boon companion, their Enkidu or Fiona MacLaren, <br /> <br /> And then if the lunars find that that is their reward for their efforts would they free the Gians of Feng-Yi? or make war on them to kill the blood of the dragons once and for all, dun dun duh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T21:27:07-07:00","id":1233600,"title":"","content":"Jumping in late to share somethimg I've wanted to do with the Caul.<br /> <br /> Seems most here want the Solars to go there to join with the Lunars against the Dragon Blooded. What I would love to do is have a Solar or a circle go their with a Dragon Blooded friend and help him/her complete the pilgrimage to be able to breed future generation of Terrestrials. Let's see some Lunar jaws drop when they realize they have a Solar standing against them here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T21:53:13-07:00","id":1233606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bb